Check that a remote aulod answers with the pinned certificate

A TLS handshake that accepts only the certificate with --pin, then a health check with the bearer
token from AULO_TOKEN when it is set. Nothing is saved.

Usage: aulo connect --pin <SHA256> <ADDR>

Arguments:
  <ADDR>
          The aulod's daemon.listen address: host:port or [ipv6]:port

Options:
      --pin <SHA256>
          The certificate's SHA-256, as aulod logs it at start; colons optional

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
